James Rising received an email from Tonima Rahman Mim, a prospective Ph.D. student interested in his Marine Science and Policy lab. She detailed her impressive academic background, highlighting her involvement in fisheries management, water pollution research, and her experience with bioaccumulation and microplastic analysis. James was asked to draft a professional response. He acknowledged her research interests and academic achievements but informed her he is not taking new students this year. He encouraged her to continue pursuing her passion and wished her well in her future endeavors.
